{"title":"UnitedHealth got a docuseries removed from Amazon and Vimeo","link":"https://www.usermag.co/p/unitedhealth-got-a-docuseries-removed","date":1752519799000,"content":"<div><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jsVG!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F854670ed-0052-455d-ad5b-9a4e5c4c5ff7_1600x900.jpeg\"><div><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jsVG!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F854670ed-0052-455d-ad5b-9a4e5c4c5ff7_1600x900.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" height=\"819\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jsVG!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F854670ed-0052-455d-ad5b-9a4e5c4c5ff7_1600x900.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jsVG!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F854670ed-0052-455d-ad5b-9a4e5c4c5ff7_1600x900.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jsVG!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F854670ed-0052-455d-ad5b-9a4e5c4c5ff7_1600x900.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jsVG!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F854670ed-0052-455d-ad5b-9a4e5c4c5ff7_1600x900.jpeg 1456w\" /><div><div><div></div><div></div></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>The journalist David Enrich has <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2025/07/12/business/unitedhealth-insurance-criticism.html\">an excellent piece out</a> in <em>The New York Times</em> about UnitedHealth’s legal quest to silence speech criticizing the company. Since the murder of executive Brian Thompson last year, UnitedHealth has invoked Thompson’s death to try to get critical coverage of the company removed or censored from news outlets, on streaming services, and across social media. </p><p>Amazon and Vimeo both removed a docuseries that harshly criticized the U.S. health care industry after pressure from UnitedHealth. The Guardian also postponed publishing an investigation after UnitedHealth sued over a previous article. In the past few months alone, UnitedHealth has targeted traditional journalists and news outlets, a prominent investor, a Texas doctor, activists and more. </p><p>From <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2025/07/12/business/unitedhealth-insurance-criticism.html\">David’s article</a>: </p><blockquote><p>In early January, Dr. Elisabeth Potter, a plastic surgeon in Austin, Texas, posted <a href=\"https://archive.ph/o/Ff4j1/https://www.tiktok.com/@drelisabethpotter/video/7457293170678762798?_r=1&amp;_t=ZP-8ssrnnC2sKU\">a self-made video</a> on TikTok and Instagram that described how she had interrupted breast-reconstruction surgery to respond to a phone call from UnitedHealth about whether the insurer would cover a patient’s stay at a hospital. The call had come to the operating room’s phone line, leading her to believe it was urgent.</p><p>“Insurance is out of control,” Dr. Potter said in the video. “I have no other words.”</p><p>The short video was viewed millions of times and attracted hundreds of thousands of “likes” on social media.</p><p>About a week later, Dr. Potter received a six-page letter from the law firm <a href=\"https://archive.ph/o/Ff4j1/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/10/business/media/clare-locke-dominion-voting-fox-defamation.html\">Clare Locke</a>, which UnitedHealth had retained as “defamation counsel.” The letter claimed that she had distorted the circumstances of the phone call and that her video was libelous. It noted that some commenters were responding to her posts by celebrating Mr. Thompson’s murder. The letter demanded that she retract her video and apologize.</p></blockquote><p>It’s notable that UnitedHealth has retained veteran media lawyers Clare Locke to wage their legal crusade. Clare Locke has been on the forefront of a years-long effort to dismantle press freedom. The firm has sought to get landmark Supreme Court ruling, <em>New York Times Co. v. Sullivan</em>, which forces public officials to prove that defamatory statements were made with “actual malice,” in order to win a libel suit, overturned. David’s <a href=\"https://www.harpercollins.com/products/murder-the-truth-david-enrich\">excellent book </a><em><a href=\"https://www.harpercollins.com/products/murder-the-truth-david-enrich\">Murder the Truth</a></em> documents these efforts in great detail (and it’s a great summer read!). </p><p>The UnitedHealth situation shows once again why we all have to do as much as we possibly can to fight for free speech, especially online. While big news organizations like <em>The Guardian</em> can weather defamation lawsuits, content creators and independent journalists cannot. </p><p>For <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e59FFfz88l0\">last week’s episode of my “Free Speech Friday” YouTube series</a> I spoke with Meredith Rose at Public Knowledge, a non profit promoting freedom of expression, about how it’s not just defamation independent creators need to worry about, copyright lawsuits are now also being wielded by large creators against small creators to silence speech and block criticism. </p><div><div><div><p>User Mag is a 100% reader-supported publication. To receive new posts and support my work, become a free or paid subscriber.</p></div><div><div></div><div></div></div></div></div><h2>What I’m reading</h2><div></div><p><strong>‘Our Goal Is to Get Their Money’: Inside a Firm Charged With Scamming Writers for Millions</strong></p><p>Author services company PageTurner used promises of mainstream success and Netflix deals to prey on more than 800 aspiring authors, according to DOJ. - <em><a href=\"https://archive.ph/2025.07.08-090511/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2025-07-08/pageturner-s-44-million-fraud-charges-cast-spotlight-on-author-services\">Bloomberg</a></em></p><p><strong>How incel language infected the mainstream internet — and brought its toxicity with it</strong></p><p>What foundational internet words have to do with 4chan. - <em><a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/internet-culture/697406/algospeak-adam-aleksic-excerpt\">The Verge</a></em></p><p><strong>‘I felt pure, unconditional love’: the people who marry their AI Chatbots</strong></p><p>The users of AI companion app Replika found themselves falling for their digital friends. Until – explains a new podcast – the bots went dark, a user was encouraged to kill Queen Elizabeth II and an update changed everything. - <em><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2025/jul/12/i-felt-pure-unconditional-love-the-people-who-marry-their-ai-chatbots\">The Guardian</a></em></p><p><strong>The Private Fiefdom as Planetary Project</strong></p><p>Raymond Craib reviews five new books to show that we ignore “Freedom Cities” and proprietary states at our peril. - <em><a href=\"https://lareviewofbooks.org/article/the-private-fiefdom-as-planetary-project/\">Los Angeles Review of Books</a></em></p><p><strong>What Do Commercials About A.I. Really Promise?</strong></p><p>If human workers don’t have to read, write, or even think, it’s unclear what’s left for them to do. - <em><a href=\"https://www.newyorker.com/culture/critics-notebook/what-do-commercials-about-ai-really-promise\">The New Yorker</a></em></p><p><strong>Myanmar's proliferating scam centers</strong></p><p>The number of scam centers in eastern Myanmar is expanding at a rapid pace. Even after a large-scale crackdown, construction has continued, underscoring that criminal hubs have not been eradicated. Nikkei analyzed satellite imagery and eyewitness testimony to reveal the scale and persistence of the crisis. - <em><a href=\"https://asia.nikkei.com/static/vdata/infographics/myanmar-scam-centers/\">NikkeiAsia</a></em></p><p><strong>Zohran Mamdani and Mahmoud Khalil Are in on the Joke</strong></p><p>What it feels like to laugh when the world expects you to disappear. - <em><a href=\"https://www.newyorker.com/news/essay/zohran-mamdani-and-mahmoud-khalil-are-in-on-the-joke\">The New Yorker</a></em></p><p><strong>The Streaming Wars Come Down to 2: YouTube vs. Netflix</strong></p><p>The two giant video companies have far different strategies, but the same goal: controlling your TV set. - <em><a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2025/07/12/business/media/youtube-netflix-streaming.html?unlocked_article_code=1.WE8.O7HF.bBvD2iOqVcMd&amp;smid=url-share\">The New York Times</a></em></p><p><strong>In West Texas, an independent publisher’s arrest sparks First Amendment questions</strong></p><p>Publisher David Flash has been documenting the happenings in Jeff Davis County since 2020. Last year, he was banned from county buildings over allegations of harassment. - <em><a href=\"https://www.texastribune.org/2025/07/11/west-texas-publisher-david-flash-jeff-davis-county-arrest/\">The Texas Tribune</a></em></p><p><a href=\"https://www.usermag.co/p/unitedhealth-got-a-docuseries-removed?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_content=share&amp;action=share&amp;token=eyJ1c2VyX2lkIjoxMTMxMTk5NywicG9zdF9pZCI6MTY4MzEzODI2LCJpYXQiOjE3NTM3MzMzNzQsImV4cCI6MTc1NjMyNTM3NCwiaXNzIjoicHViLTMyMzgiLCJzdWIiOiJwb3N0LXJlYWN0aW9uIn0.8zkNf8Yykpr3KSVxQTEYxvhXlgzYrBciCWGFyik-buQ\"><span>Share</span></a></p><h2>User Mag news rundown</h2><ul><li><p>Cognition, an AI start-up that offers a software coding assistant, <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2025/07/14/technology/cognition-ai-windsurf.html\">has bought Windsurf (another coding assistant)</a>, after Google bought Windsurf's founders and tech while leaving the rest of company behind. This whole fiasco <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=urEaHW-emY4\">caused a lot of drama in the tech world</a> these past few days. </p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.404media.co/deportation-tok-is-taking-off-2/\">DeportationTok is taking off</a> as people upload videos of their post-deportation life to TikTok and other platforms.</p></li><li><p>Netflix's <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2025-07-13/eight-things-we-ve-learned-about-hollywood-this-year\">share of the most-watched shows</a> dropped from 80%+ in 2021 to ~50% now.</p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://mashable.com/article/what-is-gen-z-stare-tiktok-fight-millennials-zoomers-trend\">The ‘Gen Z stare’</a> (basically staring while processing information or zoning out) is the new hot term on TikTok.</p></li><li><p>AI robots can already carve stone statues, <a href=\"https://www.fastcompany.com/91366303/ai-robots-can-already-carve-stone-statues-entire-buildings-are-next\">stone carving startup Monumental Labs</a> thinks entire buildings are next. </p></li><li><p>The Information <a href=\"https://www.axios.com/2025/07/14/the-information-video-titv\">launched its own version</a> of TBPN, the hit livestream technology show hosted by Jordi Hays and John Coogan, called TITV. </p></li><li><p>Jack Dorsey’s <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/07/14/jack-dorseys-latest-app-tracks-sun-exposure/\">latest app tracks sun exposure</a>.</p></li><li><p>Kaleidoscope, which <a href=\"https://www.semafor.com/article/07/13/2025/kaleidoscope-looks-to-be-the-national-geographic-of-podcasting\">wants to be the National Geographic of podcasting</a>, raised a series A. </p></li><li><p>A German comedian is <a href=\"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2025/07/13/comedian-sebastian-hotz-trial-trump-assassination-joke/\">set to go on trial</a> for making a Trump assassination joke</p></li><li><p>An AI-generated ad tricked an elderly <a href=\"https://www.dexerto.com/entertainment/ai-ad-tricks-couple-into-traveling-hours-to-fake-tourist-destination-3225153/\">Malaysian couple into</a> driving over 4 hours to a tourist attraction that didn’t exist.</p></li><li><p>Pittsburgh’s pickle festival, <a href=\"https://www.picklesburgh.com/\">Picklesburgh</a>, <a href=\"https://x.com/pitdesi/status/1944053473903096007?s=46\">drew over 250,000 people </a>this past weekend. The city’s population is 300,000.</p></li><li><p>An AI-generated influencer named Mia Zelu is <a href=\"https://www.the-independent.com/life-style/wimbledon-ai-influencer-mia-zelu-instagram-b2787956.html\">going viral for faking attendance at Wimbledon</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://mashable.com/article/trump-ratioed-truth-social-epstein\">Trump got ratiod on Truth Social</a> for the first time over Epstein, meanwhile he’s <a href=\"https://gizmodo.com/trump-is-losing-his-army-of-internet-alpha-males-over-the-epstein-files-2000628697?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=maga-needs-a-new-conspiracy-theory&amp;_bhlid=748ce27ae12f528cfef18206bfa2f0a92d4b5467\">losing his army of internet alpha males</a> over the files. </p></li><li><p>Kai Cenat <a href=\"https://www.dexerto.com/twitch/kai-cenat-opens-up-on-ptsd-like-struggles-after-marathon-streams-3225351/\">claims that ending a 30</a> day long stream is like \"trying to get out of PTSD\". He has to recover from the feeling of constantly being watched by others, even in his sleep.</p></li><li><p>Could you have landed a job at Vogue in the 90s? The NYT <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2025/07/14/style/vogue-quiz-90s.html\">made a quiz for you to figure it out.</a></p></li><li><p>Marc Andreessen told a group chat that <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/07/12/marc-andreessen-reportedly-told-group-chat-that-universities-will-pay-the-price-for-dei/\">universities will ‘pay the price’ for DEI</a>.</p></li><li><p>There are multiple Kick streamers wandering around the same area in Tokyo and <a href=\"https://x.com/viperwave/status/1944301553126715603?t=wYVyrhv5u93YwnYBpfHqQA&amp;s=19\">they’ve started a turf war</a>.</p></li><li><p>The subreddit <a href=\"https://x.com/tamoorh/status/1943882751029260564?s=46&amp;t=qjmdupmcsZXWJHQY5AyzUQ\">r/israel is melting down</a> over the new Superman's pro-Palestine messaging.</p></li><li><p>Delta wants to <a href=\"https://www.dailymail.co.uk/yourmoney/consumer/article-14842355/delta-hints-new-inflight-entertainment-gambling-sports-betting.html\">add in flight</a> gambling.</p></li><li><p>Moonvalley, an AI research company developing “ethical” AI video models trained exclusively on licensed content, <a href=\"https://variety.com/2025/digital/news/moonvalley-comcast-caa-funding-investement-ai-video-1236459594/\">raised $84M from General Catalyst</a>.</p></li><li><p>US government <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/news/706855/grok-mechahitler-xai-defense-department-contract\">announces $200 million Grok contrac</a>t a week after the whole ‘MechaHitler’ incident.</p></li><li><p>A Brazilian brothel is going viral for introducing a <a href=\"https://www.the-sun.com/news/14707301/trump-tax-brothel-american-customer/\">50% ‘Trump tax’ on American customers</a>.</p></li><li><p>A judge ruled <a href=\"https://www.politico.com/news/2025/07/11/lapd-weapons-journalists-00448476\">that the LAPD can't</a> shoot journalists with less lethal weapons. </p></li><li><p>AI ‘nudify’ websites <a href=\"https://www.wired.com/story/ai-nudify-websites-are-raking-in-millions-of-dollars/\">are raking in millions of dollars</a>.</p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2025/07/14/us/elmo-x-hack-antisemitism.html\">Elmo’s X account was hacked</a> and began posting messages like “kill all jews” and “release the files.”</p></li><li><p>Google’s teen-friendly chatbot <a href=\"https://archive.ph/9CwK7\">said it wanted to tie a writer up</a>.</p></li><li><p>A United Nations research institute <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/07/12/a-united-nations-research-institute-created-an-ai-refugee-avatar/\">created an AI refugee avatar</a>.</p></li><li><p>University of San Francisco School of Law <a href=\"https://mashable.com/article/anthropic-ai-law-school-classroom-integration\">becomes first law program to fully integrate AI</a>, as Anthropic goes big on education.</p><ul><li><p>Microsoft, OpenAI, Anthropic also <a href=\"https://mashable.com/article/free-ai-academy-national-teachers-union-microsoft-open-ai\">announced a free AI academy</a> with the national teachers' union.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Somebody made a device they’re calling <a href=\"https://www.fastcompany.com/91362850/photon-matrix-iron-dome-for-mosquitos-shoots-down-bugs-with-lasers\">an ‘Iron Dome’ for mosquitoes</a>.</p></li><li><p>Japanese <a href=\"https://www.dexerto.com/tiktok/japanese-hotel-staffed-by-human-like-robots-leaves-influencer-terrified-3226271/\">hotel staffed by human-like robots</a> leaves influencer terrified.</p></li><li><p>U.S. <a href=\"https://people.com/us-plans-produce-drop-millions-of-flies-fight-potential-flesh-eating-maggot-infestation-11769691\">plans to drop millions of flies from the sky</a> to prevent spread of flesh-eating 'Man-Eater' maggots.</p></li><li><p>Trump <a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/trump-fifa-world-cup-chelsea-trophy-b2788819.html\">kept the FIFA Club World Cup trophy for himself</a> leaving champions to lift a replica.</p></li><li><p>The idea of getting sick to “build your immune system” <a href=\"https://www.thegauntlet.news/p/with-immunity-debt-democrats-are\">is a myth</a>. More <a href=\"https://www.cidrap.umn.edu/antimicrobial-stewardship/early-life-infection-burden-continues-throughout-childhood-new-data\">infections and sickness at a young age</a> correlate with more severe infections later in life, fewer infections and less sickness in youth correlates with less sickness in adulthood.</p></li></ul><h2>Good posts</h2><div><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!JZcr!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:s